iga-surface3d-skew.out
Skew bilinear IGA surface: the tangential gradient must reproduce an affine stretch
StaticStructural nsteps 1 deltat 1.0 rtolv 1.e-11 maxiter 10 nmodules 1
errorcheck
domain 3d
OutputManager tstep_all dofman_all element_all
ndofman 4 nelem 1 ncrosssect 1 nmat 1 nbc 4 nic 0 nltf 1 nset 4
# X(xi,eta) = (xi + eta, 1.e-8 eta, 0), u = (0.1 X1, 0, 0).
# The old inverse metric loses the x component of the reciprocal xi tangent and gives F11=1.
# Both reciprocal tangents must instead reproduce F=diag(1.1,1,0) at all four Gauss points.
node 1 coords 3 0 0 0
node 2 coords 3 1 0 0
node 3 coords 3 1 1.e-8 0
node 4 coords 3 2 1.e-8 0
bspline3dsurfaceelement 1 nodes 4 1 2 3 4 crosssect 1 knotvectoru 2 0 1 knotvectorv 2 0 1 degree 2 1 1 nip 4 nlgeo 1
simplesurfacecs 1 material 1
surfacetensionmat 1 gamma1 0.5 mu 1 d 1
BoundaryCondition 1 loadTimeFunction 1 dofs 3 1 2 3 values 3 0 0 0 set 1
BoundaryCondition 2 loadTimeFunction 1 dofs 3 1 2 3 values 3 .1 0 0 set 2
BoundaryCondition 3 loadTimeFunction 1 dofs 3 1 2 3 values 3 .1 0 0 set 3
BoundaryCondition 4 loadTimeFunction 1 dofs 3 1 2 3 values 3 .2 0 0 set 4
ConstantFunction 1 f(t) 1
Set 1 nodes 1 1
Set 2 nodes 1 2
Set 3 nodes 1 3
Set 4 nodes 1 4
#%BEGIN_CHECK% tolerance 1.e-10
#ELEMENT tStep 1 number 1 irule 0 gp 1 keyword 91 component 1 value 1.1
#ELEMENT tStep 1 number 1 irule 0 gp 1 keyword 91 component 2 value 1.0
#ELEMENT tStep 1 number 1 irule 0 gp 2 keyword 91 component 1 value 1.1
#ELEMENT tStep 1 number 1 irule 0 gp 2 keyword 91 component 2 value 1.0
#ELEMENT tStep 1 number 1 irule 0 gp 3 keyword 91 component 1 value 1.1
#ELEMENT tStep 1 number 1 irule 0 gp 3 keyword 91 component 2 value 1.0
#ELEMENT tStep 1 number 1 irule 0 gp 4 keyword 91 component 1 value 1.1
#ELEMENT tStep 1 number 1 irule 0 gp 4 keyword 91 component 2 value 1.0
#%END_CHECK%
